body:
I would rephrase this comment and move it closer to the mentioned branch, e.g.
```python
if model._meta.managed:
    return True
# Check if the unmanaged model is a table.
try:
    return model._meta._is_ordinary_table
except AttributeError:
   ...
```

The reason for this comment was to highlight the reason why is this distinction necessary (PosgreSQL only supports this on ordinary tables). How about:

```python
    # PostgreSQL only supports this optimization on ordinary tables.
    def allows_group_by_selected_pks_on_model(self, model):
        # Assume that managed models are ordinary tables.
        if model._meta.managed:
            return True

        try:
            return model._meta._is_ordinary_table
        except AttributeError:
            ...
```
